; Fixture for the wasm three-state (absent / present-null / present-value) read-fidelity accessors.
; A nullable (`T / null` -> Option<T>) sitting at a wasm position that adds its OWN presence-Option is
; flattened to a single Option<T> on read (wasm-bindgen can't represent Option<Option<T>>: `Option<T>`
; is not `OptionIntoWasmAbi`). The additive presence accessors restore the lost distinction WITHOUT
; changing any existing getter signature. Each rule below exercises one lossy position:
;
;   nullable_optional_field : optional struct field   -> getter `field0()` flattens; `has_field0()` restores presence.
;   nullable_map_value      : map value               -> `get(k)` flattens; `has(k)` restores key presence.
;   nullable_enum           : single-nested enum variant -> `as_opt_u64()` flattens but is RECOVERABLE via
;                                                        `kind()` (kind says it IS the variant, so a None
;                                                        getter can only mean inner-null): docs-only, no new accessor.
;
; A DOUBLE-nested enum variant (payload resolving to Option<Option<T>>) is deliberately absent: it is
; unreachable — the wasm enum constructor panics on such a variant before any getter is emitted (see the
; `unreachable!` in generation.rs add_wasm_enum_getters), so no supported CDDL can produce it.
maybe_uint = uint / null
nullable_optional_field = [pre: uint, ? field0: maybe_uint]
nullable_map_value = { * uint => maybe_uint }
nullable_enum = tstr / (uint / null)
